      "writtenOn": "2018-10-04T19:39:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The procedure of VCC1 power-up (waking up from hibernate) reset is a superset of VCC1_RST reset.\n\nAccording to the datasheet, on VCC1 power-up reset, EC performs the following:\n* Enables the Low-Frequency Clock Generator (LFCG).\n* Loads default values to all the bits marked as “reset by VCC1 Power-Up reset”.\n* Enables all the pins powered by VCC1.\n* Performs all actions done by a VCC1_RST reset.\n\nAnd VCC1_RST reset is triggered by a low level, following a high-to-low transition.\n\nChanging it high-to-low edge is still a VCC1 power-up reset. It wakes up and EC is in some undocumented state until VCC1_RST goes high.\n\nIf we really want to a VCC1_RST reset, the only way is to do a double VCC1_RST pulse, but it seems not feasible.",
